# Static-host redirect rules (Cloudflare Pages / Netlify syntax). See landing/DEPLOY.md.
#
# The PWA is built with Vite `base: "./"`, so /app/index.html asks for `./assets/index-<hash>.js`.
# Served at the URL `/app` (no trailing slash) the document base is `/app`, and that relative URL
# resolves to `/assets/...` at the site root — every asset 404s and the page boots blank. It has
# to be a real redirect to `/app/`, not a 200 rewrite that leaves the address bar alone.
# Both hosts also do this by convention for directories; the rule makes it explicit and portable.
/app    /app/    301

# Stable public link to the Catlin reference house. The app's bundled default house *is* Catlin
# today, so this is just /app/; repoint these two rules if the default house ever changes (e.g. to
# a query param or a second bundle) and the published link keeps working.
/catlin-house     /app/    301
/catlin-house/    /app/    301

# No SPA splat rewrite: the app has no client-side router, so there are no deep links to catch,
# and a `/app/* -> /app/index.html 200` rule risks shadowing the hashed asset files it loads.
# Unknown paths fall through to 404.html. Add the splat here if routing ever lands.
